  "summary": "A new ACLU of Iowa and University of Iowa report finds 48 Iowa agencies use ALPR cameras with little state regulation, citing privacy concerns, a roughly 1-in-10 error rate, and significant spending (e.g., Cedar Rapids up to $240,000/year). The ACLU recommends cities pause adding cameras until safeguards exist.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "48 agencies now using ALPR cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "About 1 in 10 license plates recorded contain an error",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Under Iowa law, no warrant is required for law enforcement to use the ALPR database.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Cedar Rapids has spent as much as $240,000 per year in taxpayer money on the cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "our recommendation to cities is number one just don't do this",
